# Transferring a Submission to Real Duckietown {#embodied-transfer_sim_to_real status=ready}

This page describes a historical workflow for running a staged submission image on a physical Duckiebot.

The current `ente` repo set in this workspace documents the Duckiematrix simulation submission path, not direct redeployment of staged evaluator artifacts onto a robot from the public challenge server.

<div class='requirements' markdown='1'>

Requires: That you understand the distinction between the maintained simulation workflow and historical real-robot deployment workflows.

Result: You know that this page is historical context, not the maintained `ente` path.

</div>

## Current status on `ente`

- Public validation in this workspace focuses on `aido-LF-sim-validation` and the Duckiematrix simulation queue.
- Submission pages now live under `https://staging-challenges.duckietown.com/humans/submissions/![submission_number]`.
- If you need real-robot deployment, start from a maintained runtime such as the [ROS template](#ros-template) or the [Duckietown ROS baseline](#ros-baseline) and adapt that image with robot-specific tooling outside the public evaluation flow.

## Historical note

The older instructions on this topic relied on scraping evaluator artifacts and Docker Compose files from the legacy v4 challenge server. That is not the maintained `ente` workflow documented in this book.
